<title>POLAND: Universal up on Ruch bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Universal up on Ruch bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish trader Universal SA surged 9.3 percent to 11.8 zlotys in the main market's heaviest trade on hopes that a consortium which includes the firm will buy a news-stand chain  Ruch SA, traders said.</p>
<p>The treasury ministry said on Wednesday it might annul the negotiations for Ruch and launch a new one, in which a recent bid by a Polish group led by Universal could be considered, if the only bidder so far, a group led by France's Hachette fails to improve its offer.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors hope the ministry will cancel the negotiations and Universal will get Ruch,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>On Thursday Universal rose 2.9 percent.</p>
<p>Analysts said the stock was likely to fall on profit-taking in the next few sessions.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
